questions.prompt:
A library program stores each book as a record with a title (text), an author (text), a number of pages (a whole number) and a price in pounds (a decimal number).

Write, in AQA pseudo-code or a language you know:

1. a record declaration called `Book` for these four fields, with a suitable data type for each;
2. a line that creates a variable `b` holding the book *River Song* by A. Patel, 272 pages, costing 7.99;
3. a line that outputs the number of pages in `b`.
